      "sequence_position": 3,
      "problem": "Given that $P(E|G)=0.15,$ $P(E)=0.75,$ and $P(G)=0.3,$ compute $P(G|E).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(G|E) & =\\frac{P(E|G)P(G)}{P(E)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.15)(0.3)}{0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.045}{0.75} \\\\  & =0.06.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
